# netsurf: a block a script inserts or removes is placed locally
#
# Roadmap WS-C, script-driven DOM changes, second part (patch 165 did text
# edits). Measured on JS-dom-stall.html (5000 paragraphs): a paragraph
# inserted, appended at the end or removed by a script cost a rebuild of
# the whole box tree and a full layout -- 250-273 ms of stall on the host.
#
# - html.c: html_rl_block_change(), from html_reconvert_local when the
#   changed element's box holds blocks. It reconciles the element's DOM
#   children with its box children: boxes whose element left are unlinked
#   and freed (not if they hold objects, controls, frames or list
#   markers); new elements (allow-listed block tags whose content is
#   plain inline markup) are built (box_build_element), moved after the
#   box of their nearest earlier element and normalised; each change is
#   placed by layout_relayout_block. Anything it cannot take declines
#   (logged) to the full rebuild; a placement it cannot do exactly after
#   the boxes changed lays out the whole page instead (no rebuild).
# - layout.c: layout_relayout_block() places the new block (or accounts
#   for the removed one) as layout_block_context would: y = bottom of the
#   block before + its top border + the collapsed margin (the previous
#   block's bottom margin accumulated before its own top margin); what
#   follows moves by the difference, the parent and ancestors grow. Only
#   between blocks the arithmetic stands on (plain, static, unfloated,
#   uncleared, overflow visible, MAKE_HEIGHT so margins do not collapse
#   through them); at the parent's first or last place only when the
#   margin shared with the parent is unchanged.
# - box_construct.c: box_build_element() -- one new element's boxes, its
#   children bounded to it (box_build_children, shared with
#   box_rebuild_children).
# - macsurf_qjs.c: a mutation of a node that is not in the document is
#   not recorded: it has no boxes to rebuild, and recording it (a new
#   paragraph's text set before insertion) made the batch "multi", which
#   sent the insertion itself to the full rebuild.
# Sim: inserted / appended / removed paragraph placed in 5-7 ms of work,
# the longest stall of the whole test 24 ms (was 250-273 ms). Geometry
# identical to the full path: all 5001 blocks of the test page, and all
# 311 of a stress page (first-place and last-place inserts and removals,
# ten appends in one batch, two removals, and the declines: a nested
# block, a list, a paragraph holding an image).
